For the reasoning question, what actually drives understanding her decision is less an abstract rule ("family always comes first") and more her own internal experience — the anticipated guilt/regret is often the actual engine of these decisions and reflects her authentic values rather than an externally imposed hierarchy. Obligation-based framing captures something real but shouldn't be treated as an unconditional trump. Social judgment from others is the weakest ground — it may influence her, but it shouldn't be treated as a legitimate reason in itself.

